 "verdict": "ERA-CONFINED + SAME-CLASS ASTROMETRIC: the leg-separated record -- the construction that can express slip -- reproduces the same in-cap reversal as the single-fit and catalogue records, so the prospective reversal is real astrometry, not single-solution masking; the declared-axis carrier is confined to the pre-2018 record.  The post-2017 record's own dominant structure is nonetheless a lapse-slip anomaly of the same signature class on the same independent fits: single-leg rotation slip (outbound d_out_leg 0.108 vs 0.085 deg in/out, p=0.021), elevated leg disagreement (p=0.007), flat energy exchange (|daa| p=0.979), matched fit quality -- rotation without energy exchange, direction-localized at the displaced axis.  The boundary channel's registered position and leg are epoch-dependent; both eras' dominant structures are lapse-slip anomalies in the astrometric record",
 "forward_prediction": {
  "registered": "future (LSST-era) LPC cohorts continue the modern displaced-lobe polarity on the leg-separated channel; a return of the pre-2018 declared-axis inbound-leg excess, or no coherent lobe, breaks the era-polarity ordering",
  "channel": "two-leg refit d_out_leg / residual cap-gap at the displaced axis",
  "scorable_with": "this script re-run on the new cohort"
 },
